1
00:00:08,486 --> 00:00:18,012
Long long ago, in the island of Lanka,
South of ancient India, lived the evil king Ravan...

2
00:00:18,012 --> 00:00:23,169
...whose wicked ambition to
conquer and dominate the...

3
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:26,297
...whole world, caused pain
and misery to one and all.

4
00:00:27,551 --> 00:00:31,500
And in Kaushala,
a kingdom in north India...

5
00:00:31,713 --> 00:00:35,663
...people prospered under
the benevolent ruler, Dashrath.

6
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:41,906
However, Kaushala's capital
Ayodhya's biggest concern...

7
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,028
...was that King Dashrath
had no heir.

8
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:50,237
On the advice of
sage Vashishtha...

9
00:00:50,444 --> 00:00:53,353
...King Dashrath
performed a Yajna...

10
00:00:53,566 --> 00:00:55,435
...the ceremony
to beget a son.

11
00:00:56,516 --> 00:00:59,602
And as a result he was
blessed with four sons...

12
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,679
...from his three queens.

13
00:01:02,932 --> 00:01:04,801
One of them was Ram...

14
00:01:05,013 --> 00:01:06,882
...the hero of this story...

15
00:01:07,094 --> 00:01:11,045
...born of Dashrath's
first queen, Kaushalya.

16
00:01:14,207 --> 00:01:16,253
Whenever there have
been crises on the earth...

17
00:01:16,459 --> 00:01:18,328
...Lord Vishnu has
descended from the heavens...

18
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:20,410
...for its salvation.

19
00:01:21,491 --> 00:01:24,577
Lord Vishnu has
ten incarnations...

20
00:01:24,786 --> 00:01:28,736
...and Ram is believed to
be his seventh incarnation.

21
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,903
When Ram turned fifteen...

22
00:01:33,111 --> 00:01:36,019
...Ravan was at
the peak of his powers.

23
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:39,146
Ravan's relation, Marich...

24
00:01:39,355 --> 00:01:41,222
...along with his mother Tadaka...

25
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:45,386
...was a terror for sage
Vishwamitra and other hermits...

26
00:01:45,599 --> 00:01:48,507
...who lived in a forest
close to Ayodhya's border.

27
00:01:49,761 --> 00:01:52,669
They disturbed Vishwamitra's
prayers, every day.

28
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:55,796
And on one such day...

29
00:03:04,686 --> 00:03:06,554
O Lord Vishnu...

30
00:03:06,767 --> 00:03:10,718
...is there no one who can
save us from this torment?

31
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:14,879
His name is Ram.

32
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:20,076
First born prince of
King Dashrath, of Ayodhya.

33
00:04:16,489 --> 00:04:18,357
O sage of sages...

34
00:04:18,571 --> 00:04:21,479
...my court is indeed
blessed by your presence.

35
00:04:21,693 --> 00:04:23,561
What is it that
you desire of me?

36
00:04:23,775 --> 00:04:25,642
Let me fulfill your command!

37
00:04:25,855 --> 00:04:28,763
O noble king of
the Solar Dynasty...

38
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:31,885
...the demons ruined
the sacred land...

39
00:04:32,966 --> 00:04:35,012
...and we are in great trouble.
I need your...

40
00:04:35,221 --> 00:04:37,089
...eldest son Ram to destroy them.

41
00:04:41,465 --> 00:04:44,373
Ram!? He is but a mere boy.

42
00:04:44,586 --> 00:04:47,495
I, myself, shall wipe them
off from the face of this earth.

43
00:04:47,708 --> 00:04:49,576
This is a command from the Gods...

44
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:52,698
...O King, do you dare reject it?

45
00:04:52,912 --> 00:04:54,780
Dashrath, send your sons...

46
00:04:54,992 --> 00:04:56,860
...Ram and Lakshman.

47
00:04:57,074 --> 00:04:58,942
Vishwamitra is strong and wise...

48
00:05:00,024 --> 00:05:02,070
...and has mastery
over every weapon.

49
00:05:02,277 --> 00:05:04,145
He will protect your sons.

50
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,348
Ram... Lakshman...

51
00:05:09,561 --> 00:05:11,431
...come here, my sons!

52
00:05:15,805 --> 00:05:17,674
O sage Vishwamitra...

53
00:05:17,887 --> 00:05:19,755
...I leave my sons with you.

54
00:05:19,967 --> 00:05:21,836
Give them guidance and courage.

55
00:05:22,049 --> 00:05:23,918
Bless you, King Dashrath!

56
00:05:24,131 --> 00:05:28,081
You have made a decision
that shall save the world.

57
00:05:28,467 --> 00:05:31,199
We will obey you
like we obey our father.

58
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:33,284
Your wishes will
be our command.

59
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:04,508
You know, once this
was a beautiful forest...

60
00:06:04,715 --> 00:06:08,666
...but now it has dried up
because of a terrible cannibal...

61
00:06:08,878 --> 00:06:10,746
...a demoness called Tadaka.

62
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:12,827
Her son, the evil Marich...

63
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,909
...leads the demons...

64
00:06:15,122 --> 00:06:16,989
...who defile the holy fires.

65
00:06:17,203 --> 00:06:19,071
Ram, you must kill Tadaka.

66
00:06:19,284 --> 00:06:21,152
That is your dharma!

67
00:06:21,366 --> 00:06:23,233
Your duty as a Kshatriya!

68
00:06:24,315 --> 00:06:26,360
I shall teach you Mantras...

69
00:06:26,568 --> 00:06:28,436
They will guide you.

70
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:31,558
Now... repeat after me.

71
00:06:49,289 --> 00:06:51,335
Stop it!

72
00:06:53,452 --> 00:06:57,568
That mantra tears apart...

73
00:07:27,794 --> 00:07:30,880
Ram, use the mantra.
Recite the mantra!

74
00:08:14,794 --> 00:08:16,662
Many years ago...

75
00:08:16,876 --> 00:08:18,744
...in this very place...

76
00:08:19,825 --> 00:08:22,945
...the Gods rewarded
my long years of penance...

77
00:08:23,155 --> 00:08:26,095
...with the mastery
of supreme weapons.

78
00:08:27,363 --> 00:08:29,251
The time has now come...

79
00:08:29,466 --> 00:08:31,354
...for me to pass
on these weapons...

80
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:33,458
...to one worthy of them.

81
00:08:38,933 --> 00:08:41,873
Take them, Ram,
and use them well.

82
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:53,448
They are now yours.

83
00:08:53,659 --> 00:08:55,547
Use them to protect 'Dharma'.

84
00:09:14,697 --> 00:09:18,689
That's him!
The one who killed my mother.

85
00:09:18,904 --> 00:09:20,792
I shall avenge
her with his blood...

86
00:09:21,008 --> 00:09:22,896
...this I swear!

87
00:09:26,093 --> 00:09:28,161
Watch out!

88
00:10:02,031 --> 00:10:03,920
You used the divine weapons!

89
00:10:04,135 --> 00:10:06,024
How did you learn so soon?

90
00:10:06,238 --> 00:10:08,127
These are the weapons of the Gods.

91
00:10:10,272 --> 00:10:13,392
And the righteous one needs
no lessons to use them.

92
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:16,543
Show me, my Guru...

93
00:10:16,758 --> 00:10:18,646
...how to use this Chakra?

94
00:10:18,862 --> 00:10:21,801
You will learn but only
if you pursue your destiny...

95
00:10:22,018 --> 00:10:23,906
...in righteousness.

96
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:39,688
Listen all!

97
00:10:39,899 --> 00:10:42,839
This is the great bow of Shiva!

98
00:10:43,055 --> 00:10:44,943
He who lifts it and strings it...

99
00:10:46,036 --> 00:10:49,155
...shall receive a
great reward from King Janak.

100
00:10:50,418 --> 00:10:52,306
The winner shall be given...

101
00:10:52,521 --> 00:10:54,409
...the hand of Princess Sita.

102
00:10:54,625 --> 00:10:56,513
...in marriage.

103
00:11:25,129 --> 00:11:28,070
Next, Prince Jagtara of Sorav.

104
00:11:47,745 --> 00:11:51,739
Next, the Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

105
00:12:48,754 --> 00:12:51,695
Congratulations on
your wedding, Prince Ram.

106
00:13:10,844 --> 00:13:12,732
Years passed.

107
00:13:12,948 --> 00:13:14,836
Ayodhya grew and prospered.

108
00:13:15,052 --> 00:13:16,940
And the people loved Ram.

109
00:13:18,031 --> 00:13:20,099
Their prince and king-to-be.

110
00:13:20,311 --> 00:13:22,199
The four brothers live in harmony...

111
00:13:22,415 --> 00:13:25,354
...and their future looks full of hope.

112
00:13:28,726 --> 00:13:31,666
My people, this morning I awoke
from a dream full of omens.

113
00:13:31,881 --> 00:13:33,770
Guru Vashishtha sees in them...

114
00:13:33,985 --> 00:13:35,873
...the coming of troubled times.

115
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:40,080
But my health is failing...

116
00:13:40,297 --> 00:13:42,185
I am getting old and...

117
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,288
...have no more power
to resist those evil forces.

118
00:13:45,379 --> 00:13:47,447
I have, therefore, decided...

119
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,548
...that Ram will succeed me.

120
00:13:50,815 --> 00:13:52,703
He will be the
next king of Ayodhya.

121
00:13:52,918 --> 00:13:55,859
Ram, my son, come forward.

122
00:14:01,334 --> 00:14:04,269
Ram, try to live up
to the people's expectations.

123
00:14:04,484 --> 00:14:06,369
I have faith in you.

124
00:14:06,583 --> 00:14:08,468
I will do my utmost...

125
00:14:08,683 --> 00:14:10,568
...to live up to the
ideals you have set for us.

126
00:14:10,782 --> 00:14:12,668
Long live Ayodhya!

127
00:14:12,882 --> 00:14:14,768
Long live King Dashrath!

128
00:14:14,983 --> 00:14:16,868
Long live Prince Ram!

129
00:14:27,406 --> 00:14:29,470
Get away... get away.

130
00:14:29,681 --> 00:14:32,616
Noisy wretched things!

131
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:34,716
Manthara, stop abusing the birds.

132
00:14:35,806 --> 00:14:37,870
Aah... Kekeyi, is this the time...

133
00:14:38,079 --> 00:14:39,965
...to beautify yourself?

134
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:43,114
When great misfortune
creeps upon the kingdom?

135
00:14:43,330 --> 00:14:46,264
Manthara, don't you understand?

136
00:14:50,504 --> 00:14:52,568
Our beloved Ram is to be anointed...

137
00:14:52,778 --> 00:14:54,663
...crown prince tomorrow.

138
00:14:54,879 --> 00:14:57,813
And so I said,
it is a misfortune.

139
00:14:58,028 --> 00:15:00,962
Oh Kekeyi...

140
00:15:01,178 --> 00:15:03,062
...you are so innocent!

141
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,162
So trusting! And look...

142
00:15:05,377 --> 00:15:09,362
...look how King Dashrath
has betrayed your trust!?

143
00:15:09,577 --> 00:15:11,461
Hold your tongue, Manthara.

144
00:15:11,677 --> 00:15:13,561
I will never allow you to
speak of the King in this way.

145
00:15:13,776 --> 00:15:15,660
Why? Why do you think...

146
00:15:15,876 --> 00:15:18,810
...the king sent Bharat away, now?

147
00:15:19,026 --> 00:15:20,910
So conveniently...

148
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:24,059
... before the coronation! Why!?

149
00:15:25,324 --> 00:15:28,259
Why? I wonder why he did that?

150
00:15:30,399 --> 00:15:33,512
Kaushalya might have suggested it...

151
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:35,608
...to the king. Yes!

152
00:15:35,823 --> 00:15:38,758
You know you are the
king's favorite queen...

153
00:15:38,973 --> 00:15:41,908
...and Kaushalya hates you for that.

154
00:15:42,123 --> 00:15:44,007
She is jealous... jealous...

155
00:15:44,223 --> 00:15:47,157
...of your youth
and beauty, aah!

156
00:15:48,422 --> 00:15:50,306
What can I do?

157
00:15:50,521 --> 00:15:52,406
Leave everything...

158
00:15:52,621 --> 00:15:55,555
...to this loyal
and clever Manthara.

159
00:16:19,918 --> 00:16:21,804
What's happened?

160
00:16:23,068 --> 00:16:24,954
Why this sorrow, this anger...

161
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:27,053
...on such an auspicious night?

162
00:16:27,267 --> 00:16:29,153
What can I do?
Come, tell me.

163
00:16:29,367 --> 00:16:32,303
Tell me O King,
do you remember when you were...

164
00:16:32,516 --> 00:16:34,402
...injured in a
battle some years ago?

165
00:16:43,015 --> 00:16:44,901
I drove you to safety...

166
00:16:45,990 --> 00:16:50,143
...and you promised to
fulfill two boons of mine.

167
00:16:54,565 --> 00:16:56,449
You must grant me...

168
00:16:56,665 --> 00:16:58,549
...those two boons, now!

169
00:16:58,765 --> 00:17:00,649
Only two boons!?

170
00:17:02,789 --> 00:17:04,853
You can have more,
if you want.

171
00:17:05,063 --> 00:17:06,948
No, I don't need more than two.

172
00:17:08,037 --> 00:17:10,101
The first is...

173
00:17:12,238 --> 00:17:14,302
No... I cannot grant you...

174
00:17:14,513 --> 00:17:16,397
...those, Kekeyi. Not those!

175
00:17:16,613 --> 00:17:19,547
I will give you all my wealth.
Will that please you? - No.

176
00:17:21,686 --> 00:17:23,750
Do you wanted to be known...

177
00:17:23,962 --> 00:17:26,896
...that a king of Solar Dynasty
went back on his words.

178
00:17:27,111 --> 00:17:28,996
I will be content...

179
00:17:29,211 --> 00:17:32,145
...with only those two boons.

180
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:37,395
The boons were...

181
00:17:38,484 --> 00:17:41,598
...one, Kekeyi's son,
Bharat, to be made king...

182
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,744
...and two,
Ram to be banished...

183
00:17:44,959 --> 00:17:47,893
...to the forest
for fourteen years.

184
00:17:50,033 --> 00:17:52,097
Brother, can you not hear
the people's voices?

185
00:17:52,308 --> 00:17:55,242
Lakshman, this
is part of my fate.

186
00:17:55,458 --> 00:17:58,392
But are we, on that
account to sit still...

187
00:17:58,607 --> 00:18:00,491
...and do nothing?
This sword...

188
00:18:00,707 --> 00:18:02,579
...is it only an ornament,
just a plaything?

189
00:18:02,792 --> 00:18:05,708
Brother, you are part
of my self, sharing...

190
00:18:05,921 --> 00:18:07,793
...the same soul with me.
Please...

191
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:10,925
...try to understand me.

192
00:18:11,134 --> 00:18:13,007
My Lord, I am
coming with you.

193
00:18:14,784 --> 00:18:16,135
But Sita, you...

194
00:18:18,434 --> 00:18:21,349
A husband's duty
is his wife's too.

195
00:18:21,563 --> 00:18:23,434
Your fate is equally mine.
- That's right!

196
00:18:26,777 --> 00:18:28,648
And the same soul should
follow the same fate.

197
00:18:28,862 --> 00:18:31,776
And so brother, I, too,
am coming with you.

198
00:18:34,944 --> 00:18:36,995
Thank you!

199
00:18:47,458 --> 00:18:49,508
Mother... take heart!

200
00:18:49,717 --> 00:18:51,589
Fourteen years will
pass very quickly.

201
00:18:51,802 --> 00:18:55,761
And I will be back, seeking your
blessings in no time at all.

202
00:18:55,973 --> 00:18:57,846
Yes, my son. - Ram!

203
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:11,405
Ram, why don't
you blame me?

204
00:19:11,615 --> 00:19:13,488
Why don't you bear
a grudge against me?

205
00:19:13,701 --> 00:19:15,573
That would ease my guilt.

206
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:19,748
I don't want the kingdom.
Nor the power.

207
00:19:19,957 --> 00:19:23,916
All I want are your blessings
before we depart. Father!

208
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,090
My son, bring glory to our
great line of kings.

209
00:19:28,299 --> 00:19:30,172
Come back safe.

210
00:19:33,513 --> 00:19:36,428
Who in the world can
boast of a son like you?

211
00:19:40,813 --> 00:19:42,684
Sumantra...

212
00:19:44,984 --> 00:19:47,898
...get ready the chariots,
the elephants, horses and...

213
00:19:48,112 --> 00:19:49,985
...foot soldiers to accompany
Ram to the forest.

214
00:19:50,198 --> 00:19:52,070
Yes, your majesty!

215
00:19:52,283 --> 00:19:55,198
Father, when nature herself
will take care of me...

216
00:19:55,411 --> 00:19:58,327
...what use I have of an army,
of royal pageantry?

217
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:01,455
Of course, you will
give Bharat this kingdom...

218
00:20:01,668 --> 00:20:04,583
...after draining it
of all its wealth.

219
00:20:24,609 --> 00:20:27,524
Mother, give your blessings
to your departing son.

220
00:20:37,991 --> 00:20:40,041
Ram, don't leave us.

221
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:43,165
Remain as our king.
- Beloved citizens...

222
00:20:44,248 --> 00:20:46,298
You know how
much I love you.

223
00:20:46,507 --> 00:20:48,379
And I know how much
you love me.

224
00:20:48,592 --> 00:20:50,465
You will show your
love for me by...

225
00:20:50,679 --> 00:20:52,550
...loving my noble brother, Bharat...

226
00:20:52,764 --> 00:20:55,678
...who is fully worthy of your
love and of being your king.

227
00:20:56,935 --> 00:20:59,849
Support him, I beg of you. Support...

228
00:21:00,932 --> 00:21:04,025
...my sorrowful father. People
of Ayodhya, I appeal to you.

229
00:21:05,103 --> 00:21:08,196
Ram... don't go, Ram, Please.

230
00:21:25,958 --> 00:21:28,008
Ram... come back soon!

231
00:21:34,475 --> 00:21:36,346
O my son!

232
00:21:37,603 --> 00:21:39,474
Ram!

233
00:21:40,627 --> 00:21:41,563
Take care...

234
00:21:41,774 --> 00:21:44,689
...Ram, Lakshman, Sita!

235
00:21:44,902 --> 00:21:46,775
You take care too.

236
00:21:46,988 --> 00:21:49,903
And please, look after my father.

237
00:21:50,116 --> 00:21:51,988
I will.

238
00:22:43,123 --> 00:22:45,173
RAM!!!

239
00:23:03,005 --> 00:23:04,985
Six months passed by.

240
00:23:05,195 --> 00:23:07,068
King Dashrath's palace is...

241
00:23:07,281 --> 00:23:09,153
...enveloped in darkness.

242
00:23:09,366 --> 00:23:11,239
Ram...

243
00:23:12,321 --> 00:23:14,371
...forgive your father.

244
00:23:14,580 --> 00:23:16,452
Ram... Ram!

245
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:25,838
He is free from the
sufferings of this world.

246
00:23:31,090 --> 00:23:33,140
Bharat, Kekeyi's son...

247
00:23:33,350 --> 00:23:35,223
...who was away in Kekeya...

248
00:23:35,436 --> 00:23:37,308
...visiting his grandfather...

249
00:23:37,521 --> 00:23:40,436
...was called back to Ayodhya.

250
00:24:07,587 --> 00:24:09,637
Mother... mother! What is this?
What has happened?

251
00:24:10,716 --> 00:24:13,809
Oh Bharat, you have come at last.

252
00:24:14,018 --> 00:24:17,977
Tell me mother, is it true,
father has passed away?

253
00:24:19,058 --> 00:24:21,108
Oh God!

254
00:24:22,187 --> 00:24:24,237
Then it is true! - Yes.

255
00:24:24,446 --> 00:24:27,361
But he left us a great honor.
- What is it?

256
00:24:33,831 --> 00:24:36,745
What have you done,
you depraved heartless woman?

257
00:24:39,045 --> 00:24:41,959
What perverse tongue
poisoned your mind?

258
00:24:42,173 --> 00:24:44,045
Brother, it is she.

259
00:24:44,259 --> 00:24:47,173
It is this evil wretch
who has sown the...

260
00:24:47,387 --> 00:24:50,302
...seed of madness
in our mother's heart.

261
00:24:50,515 --> 00:24:52,387
Please...

262
00:24:52,601 --> 00:24:54,473
...please forgive me.

263
00:24:55,555 --> 00:24:58,648
I was only thinking of you two...

264
00:24:58,857 --> 00:25:01,772
...Kekeyi and Bharat's...
- Stop it.

265
00:25:01,985 --> 00:25:05,944
I will cleave your filthy
brain in two. - That's enough.

266
00:25:06,156 --> 00:25:09,071
Don't let her blood
defile our father's soul.

267
00:25:10,327 --> 00:25:13,242
You are no longer my mother...

268
00:25:13,456 --> 00:25:15,328
...let the world know it.

269
00:25:16,410 --> 00:25:18,460
Please forgive me...

270
00:25:18,670 --> 00:25:21,584
...forgive your
poor mother, Bharat...

271
00:25:21,798 --> 00:25:24,712
...please, forgive me.

272
00:25:26,838 --> 00:25:28,889
Forgive me!

273
00:25:37,336 --> 00:25:38,271
What?

274
00:25:39,352 --> 00:25:41,401
What are you saying, Bharat?

275
00:25:41,610 --> 00:25:44,526
Our father is dead!?

276
00:25:44,739 --> 00:25:46,611
Brother...

277
00:25:46,824 --> 00:25:48,697
...I share your grief.

278
00:25:56,210 --> 00:25:58,081
Father... father...

279
00:25:59,164 --> 00:26:01,214
...forgive this poor Ram...

280
00:26:01,424 --> 00:26:03,296
...forgive your son, please.

281
00:26:04,552 --> 00:26:06,424
Ram, I appeal to you...

282
00:26:06,637 --> 00:26:08,510
...absolve me of my mother's sin.

283
00:26:08,723 --> 00:26:12,682
Come back to Ayodhya and accept...

284
00:26:12,894 --> 00:26:14,766
...the kingdom which is
yours by right. - Bharat...

285
00:26:14,979 --> 00:26:16,852
...what your mother has done
is not in question here.

286
00:26:17,065 --> 00:26:21,024
Remember, the great Emperor
Dashrath has commanded us...

287
00:26:22,105 --> 00:26:25,198
...you to rule the kingdom and I...

288
00:26:25,407 --> 00:26:27,279
...to live in this forest
for fourteen years.

289
00:26:27,493 --> 00:26:30,407
It is our duty to abide
by our father's wishes...

290
00:26:30,621 --> 00:26:32,493
...whether we like it or not.

291
00:26:32,707 --> 00:26:34,578
You have commanded me,
it is enough.

292
00:26:34,792 --> 00:26:36,664
But one thing is certain.

293
00:26:36,878 --> 00:26:39,792
I will not accept
the kingdom for myself.

294
00:26:40,006 --> 00:26:41,878
But for you!

295
00:26:45,220 --> 00:26:47,092
Please bless this
brother of yours...

296
00:26:47,305 --> 00:26:50,220
...to rule the kingdom with
strength and courage.

297
00:27:00,861 --> 00:27:02,733
I will rule for the
next fourteen years...

298
00:27:02,946 --> 00:27:04,819
...but only till you return.

299
00:27:05,033 --> 00:27:08,469
Bharat, my brother. - Ram.

300
00:27:08,681 --> 00:27:10,731
Long live Ram.

301
00:27:10,941 --> 00:27:13,156
Long live Bharat.

302
00:28:17,852 --> 00:28:19,904
What brings my
chief minister out here...

303
00:28:20,114 --> 00:28:21,987
...at this unlikely hour?

304
00:28:22,202 --> 00:28:25,119
Sir, in the forest of
Dandaka and Janasthana...

305
00:28:25,333 --> 00:28:28,250
...they say the holy men are
returning to their ashrams.

306
00:28:28,464 --> 00:28:30,337
They seem to have
gained a new confidence.

307
00:28:30,552 --> 00:28:33,469
Our spies say, it is
the doing of the young...

308
00:28:33,683 --> 00:28:35,556
...prince of Ayodhya,
Prince Ram.

309
00:28:37,683 --> 00:28:41,811
Oh, this boy Ram is
handsome, isn't he?

310
00:28:42,902 --> 00:28:44,954
I've heard this
Ram is a cowards...

311
00:28:45,163 --> 00:28:48,081
...who has been sent into
exile by his own people.

312
00:28:48,294 --> 00:28:50,168
That's right,
my king, but we must...

313
00:28:50,382 --> 00:28:52,256
...do something before
it is too late.

314
00:28:53,513 --> 00:28:57,476
Oh Ram, I can't
wait to see you.

315
00:31:38,597 --> 00:31:40,471
Shurpankha, Ravan's
younger sister...

316
00:31:40,685 --> 00:31:44,647
.disguised as a beautiful
lady comes to Panchvati...

317
00:31:44,860 --> 00:31:46,733
...to entice Ram.

318
00:31:47,991 --> 00:31:50,908
I am Shurpankha.

319
00:31:56,166 --> 00:31:58,218
Ram, you are so beautiful...

320
00:31:59,298 --> 00:32:01,350
...strong and handsome.

321
00:32:01,560 --> 00:32:03,433
I have decided to marry you.

322
00:32:05,735 --> 00:32:07,608
Your wish would be my command...

323
00:32:07,822 --> 00:32:09,695
...were it not for my
wife Sita, there.

324
00:32:09,910 --> 00:32:12,827
Why don't you approach
my brother, Lakshman?

325
00:32:13,041 --> 00:32:15,958
He is also very handsome
and very strong.

326
00:32:16,172 --> 00:32:19,089
Hmm... he is handsome too.

327
00:32:19,303 --> 00:32:22,220
I speak with your interest at
heart. I am only second to Ram.

328
00:32:22,434 --> 00:32:26,396
And I don't think you are the
kind to settle for second best!?

329
00:32:26,609 --> 00:32:28,483
Yes, you are right!

330
00:32:29,566 --> 00:32:32,662
I am the kind to settle only
for the very best.

331
00:32:33,741 --> 00:32:37,869
Come... come. I will introduce
you to... this is my wife Sita.

332
00:32:38,384 --> 00:32:44,434
This ugly one is your
wife!? I will kill her.

333
00:32:56,877 --> 00:32:58,751
Oh... my nose.

334
00:33:00,008 --> 00:33:01,882
My nose!!

335
00:33:02,966 --> 00:33:05,018
Bleeding!

336
00:33:07,141 --> 00:33:10,237
O the Energy which bestows
knowledge to conquer...

337
00:33:10,446 --> 00:33:13,364
...the phenomenon of death...
may please rise... rise...

338
00:33:13,577 --> 00:33:17,540
...and bestow your
blessings! Swaha!

339
00:33:20,708 --> 00:33:22,760
Brother! - What's
happened to you?

340
00:33:22,970 --> 00:33:25,887
O our little sister!
What has happened!?

341
00:33:29,058 --> 00:33:32,154
Ram!? You mean that... that...
puny prince from Ayodhya!?

342
00:33:32,364 --> 00:33:35,281
Is he the one
who attacked you?

343
00:33:36,236 --> 00:33:50,000
Those you call... puny princes...
...have insulted you...

344
00:33:50,108 --> 00:33:51,981
Do not worry, little sister.

345
00:33:52,195 --> 00:33:55,112
I will have these
worms sliced up and...

346
00:33:55,326 --> 00:33:57,200
...and feed the
ravens for breakfast.

347
00:33:57,414 --> 00:33:59,287
Where is my brother Kumbhakarna?

348
00:33:59,501 --> 00:34:02,418
Tell him, I have said, he
must lead the attack.

349
00:34:24,551 --> 00:34:26,424
Just as I feared, my King...

350
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:29,556
...your brother Kumbhakarna won't
wake up for the next six months.

351
00:34:29,770 --> 00:34:33,732
That Sita... I wish I
could destroy her beauty.

352
00:34:34,814 --> 00:34:36,866
Is she... that beautiful?

353
00:34:37,945 --> 00:34:42,073
There is no one more beautiful
than her in this whole world.

354
00:34:45,425 --> 00:34:49,388
Her waist is slim,
her figure captivating...

355
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:53,563
...her complexion
like molten gold.

356
00:34:55,862 --> 00:35:00,869
A heavenly maid who is
designed for you, my brother.

357
00:35:01,081 --> 00:35:02,955
She is not worthy of that Ram.

358
00:35:04,212 --> 00:35:07,130
There surely is someone
who is worthy of her.

359
00:35:07,344 --> 00:35:10,262
And that someone is you.

360
00:35:42,656 --> 00:35:45,752
Ravan, accompanied by
his uncle Marich...

361
00:35:45,962 --> 00:35:47,835
...sets out to kidnap Sita.

362
00:35:49,093 --> 00:35:52,010
Then... as we planned?

363
00:35:52,224 --> 00:35:56,186
Yes, as we planned!

364
00:36:01,444 --> 00:36:03,496
This is magnificent!!!

365
00:36:04,575 --> 00:36:07,670
And this can
surely deceive Ram.

366
00:36:20,231 --> 00:36:22,283
Oh... how beautiful she is!

367
00:36:28,755 --> 00:36:31,672
Oh! How lovely!

368
00:36:31,887 --> 00:36:34,804
It 'is' real, isn't it?
It's not a dream, is it?

369
00:36:35,018 --> 00:36:37,935
O Ram, won't you
capture the deer for me?

370
00:36:38,149 --> 00:36:41,066
It is the most beautiful
thing I've ever seen.

371
00:36:41,280 --> 00:36:44,197
For you? I will!
Lakshman, look after Sita.

372
00:36:51,718 --> 00:36:54,635
Brother, remember that this
deer's beauty is Marich.

373
00:36:54,849 --> 00:36:57,766
Watch out! Watch out for
those treacherous creatures.

374
00:36:57,980 --> 00:36:59,853
All right! Protect Sita.

375
00:37:10,504 --> 00:37:13,422
So, it is a demon,
disguised as a deer!

376
00:37:23,029 --> 00:37:26,992
You might be relieved
that you have killed me.

377
00:37:27,204 --> 00:37:30,122
But you better be worried
about your pretty wife.

378
00:37:30,335 --> 00:37:33,253
What? - Lakshman, Sita...

379
00:37:33,466 --> 00:37:35,341
...help me!

380
00:37:37,641 --> 00:37:40,559
Lakshman, did you hear
that dreadful cry?

381
00:37:40,772 --> 00:37:43,690
Ram is in danger.
He needs your help.

382
00:37:43,904 --> 00:37:46,822
O he will be safe.
Don't worry, sister.

383
00:37:47,035 --> 00:37:49,953
What are you saying?
You wish him dead?

384
00:37:51,210 --> 00:37:54,128
I understand, so,
I will obey you!

385
00:38:06,866 --> 00:38:09,811
Sister, do not step
outside this line.

386
00:38:10,027 --> 00:38:12,972
Within this line you
are safe. I assure you.

387
00:38:21,617 --> 00:38:25,617
Everything goes
just as I planned.

388
00:38:49,890 --> 00:38:53,015
Om Namah Shivay!
(Obeisance to Lord Shiva!)

389
00:38:55,334 --> 00:38:57,225
O virtuous lady...

390
00:38:58,319 --> 00:39:00,391
...I come begging for alms.

391
00:39:16,407 --> 00:39:18,298
Here you are.

392
00:39:21,676 --> 00:39:23,567
Oh, I am surprised.

393
00:39:23,782 --> 00:39:26,727
Somebody has drawn it
to protect you.

394
00:39:26,943 --> 00:39:29,888
I cannot cross it but
you surely can. Come.

395
00:39:30,982 --> 00:39:33,054
No... no.

396
00:39:33,266 --> 00:39:37,266
If you do not feed this hungry
saint with your hands...

397
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:42,533
...then ruin shall fall upon
your father's and father-in-law's house...

398
00:39:42,748 --> 00:39:44,640
...O noble lady!

399
00:39:50,595 --> 00:39:56,344
Come closer, O noble lady,
And you shall recieve my blessings.

400
00:40:19,158 --> 00:40:22,249
Lakshman!? - Ram! - Why did
you leave Sita alone?

401
00:40:22,458 --> 00:40:25,371
Why are you here? - She
insisted I leave when we heard your cry.

402
00:40:25,585 --> 00:40:29,541
Oh no! That was the voice of
demon imitating mine.

403
00:40:29,752 --> 00:40:31,623
I fear the worst. Come...

404
00:40:31,837 --> 00:40:33,707
...let's get back
as soon as we can.

405
00:40:35,831 --> 00:40:37,880
Ram... Ram!

406
00:40:43,300 --> 00:40:45,170
Rescue me!

407
00:40:49,378 --> 00:40:52,470
Lakshman... Ram... help me!

408
00:40:53,547 --> 00:40:54,552
Sita!

409
00:40:55,804 --> 00:41:00,802
You are mine now. - No... no...
Jatayu, help me. No!!

410
00:41:09,351 --> 00:41:12,263
Let her go. She does
not belong to you.

411
00:41:21,856 --> 00:41:23,727
Let me go. Oh!

412
00:41:30,192 --> 00:41:32,063
Jatayu...

413
00:41:41,481 --> 00:41:42,487
Will teach him a lesson.

414
00:41:45,649 --> 00:41:47,698
Jatayu...

415
00:41:51,033 --> 00:41:52,903
Let me go.

416
00:41:53,118 --> 00:41:56,031
No one can save you now.

417
00:42:09,617 --> 00:42:11,666
He tricked me!

418
00:42:11,874 --> 00:42:14,787
He tricked me and abducted my
wife during my absence.

419
00:42:17,086 --> 00:42:19,998
I swear, Lakshman, I swear.
I shall try to vanquish him.

420
00:42:21,079 --> 00:42:24,171
I shall follow that fellow
into the ends of the universe.

421
00:42:24,379 --> 00:42:26,250
I will seek him out.

422
00:42:26,463 --> 00:42:29,376
And I... will destroy him.

423
00:42:31,674 --> 00:42:34,587
Calm down, my brother Ram.
You have always said that...

424
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:37,712
...anger is not the right
path to justice.

425
00:42:37,926 --> 00:42:40,838
You, who have only the good
of the world at heart...

426
00:42:41,053 --> 00:42:43,966
...must not let anger
plunge you into it.

427
00:42:46,089 --> 00:42:48,138
You are right...
you are right, Lakshman.

428
00:42:49,215 --> 00:42:52,306
Now, it is your turn to lead...

429
00:42:52,515 --> 00:42:55,428
...my little brother
and I will follow.

430
00:42:56,509 --> 00:42:58,558
Lakshman, is this
gentle creature...

431
00:42:58,767 --> 00:43:00,638
...trying to tell us
something about Sita?

432
00:43:00,852 --> 00:43:03,764
It might be showing us
the direction...

433
00:43:03,978 --> 00:43:05,848
...in which Sita has been
taken. Let's go.

434
00:43:06,062 --> 00:43:10,018
Help me! Ram... Ram!!!

435
00:43:14,398 --> 00:43:16,269
Hey, what is this?

436
00:43:19,608 --> 00:43:21,479
Forgive me, Ram...

437
00:43:21,693 --> 00:43:24,588
...I tried to stop him,
but he carried her away.

438
00:43:24,800 --> 00:43:27,694
My old wings were too frail.

439
00:43:27,907 --> 00:43:30,801
Oh Jatayu...

440
00:43:31,013 --> 00:43:32,872
...how can I blame you?

441
00:43:33,947 --> 00:43:37,019
You have given your life's
blood for my beloved wife!

442
00:43:37,227 --> 00:43:41,158
Do not lose heart, Ram.
You will find her again.

443
00:43:41,369 --> 00:43:44,265
Jatayu... Jatayu...

444
00:43:50,690 --> 00:43:52,549
Where are you taking me?

445
00:43:53,624 --> 00:43:55,660
Let me go.

446
00:44:10,366 --> 00:44:13,260
Remember all of you. If anyone
tries to harm her...

447
00:44:13,474 --> 00:44:16,368
...they will die. This lady
here is so noble...

448
00:44:16,580 --> 00:44:19,474
...that even looking at you
makes her impure.

449
00:44:20,549 --> 00:44:22,585
Trijata!? - What does Your Majesty wish of me?

450
00:44:22,793 --> 00:44:24,653
I appoint you her keeper.

451
00:44:24,865 --> 00:44:26,724
Whatever she asks for
in the Ashok Van...

452
00:44:27,798 --> 00:44:29,835
...see that she gets it.
- Very well, your Majesty.

453
00:44:30,042 --> 00:44:33,973
She is stubborn. But you must
give her everything she wants.

454
00:44:34,185 --> 00:44:36,044
Except freedom!

455
00:44:52,722 --> 00:44:54,687
Could it be...

456
00:44:54,897 --> 00:44:58,828
...human blood? Yum... yum... yum.

457
00:44:59,040 --> 00:45:00,898
So good!

458
00:45:04,044 --> 00:45:06,080
An arrow!? Painful
if it hits me.

459
00:45:08,186 --> 00:45:10,223
But it doesn't hit me.

460
00:45:15,437 --> 00:45:17,472
I got her!

461
00:45:50,819 --> 00:45:55,787
Thank you! I was a heavenly
creature, cursed to be...

462
00:45:55,998 --> 00:45:58,893
...an ugly demon. And no one
could lift the curse.

463
00:45:59,104 --> 00:46:01,999
Only if I were defeated by
a man of justice...

464
00:46:02,211 --> 00:46:06,142
...I could regain my original
self and go back to the heavens.

465
00:46:07,217 --> 00:46:09,253
Thank you, Ram. But...

466
00:46:09,461 --> 00:46:11,320
...there is nothing I can do
for you in return, except...

467
00:46:11,531 --> 00:46:14,426
...give you advice.

468
00:46:14,638 --> 00:46:17,533
Find Sugriva now.

469
00:46:18,608 --> 00:46:20,645
Sugriva!? Who is he?

470
00:46:26,030 --> 00:46:27,889
It's a lake.

471
00:46:28,964 --> 00:46:31,000
Lakshman, now what do we do?

472
00:46:31,209 --> 00:46:34,103
There seems to be someone over
there. Let's go and...

473
00:46:34,314 --> 00:46:36,174
...ask them about Sugriva.
- That's a good idea.

474
00:46:40,529 --> 00:46:42,388
Wait!

475
00:46:52,957 --> 00:46:55,851
And in the great
mother's magic play...

476
00:46:56,062 --> 00:46:58,957
...all of us perform
our little roles.

477
00:47:01,241 --> 00:47:05,172
I never thought I could see a
man of knowledge like you...

478
00:47:05,384 --> 00:47:08,328
...in this wilderness. My name
is Ram and this is my brother Lakshman.

479
00:47:08,542 --> 00:47:10,432
We are the sons of
King Dashrath of Ayodhya.

480
00:47:10,648 --> 00:47:14,646
We come in search of my
beloved wife, Sita...

481
00:47:14,861 --> 00:47:16,752
...who has been carried
away by a demon...

482
00:47:16,968 --> 00:47:18,858
...I know not, where?

483
00:47:19,073 --> 00:47:22,017
Indeed it is a benevolent
destiny that leads me...

484
00:47:22,233 --> 00:47:24,124
...to Prince Ram of Ayodhya.

485
00:47:26,270 --> 00:47:29,394
My name is Hanuman.

486
00:47:29,605 --> 00:47:32,549
And I am minister to
the King Sugriva.

487
00:47:32,764 --> 00:47:36,762
Lakshman, we've been wondering
where to find Sugriva...

488
00:47:36,977 --> 00:47:39,921
...and here is Sugriva's
messenger welcoming us.

489
00:47:40,137 --> 00:47:43,080
Indeed kind destiny
has guided us here.

490
00:47:44,173 --> 00:47:46,243
Ram... Lakshman...

491
00:47:46,455 --> 00:47:49,398
...it is indeed an honor to meet
the sons of King Dashrath...

492
00:47:49,615 --> 00:47:52,559
...whose greatness is known in
all four corners of the world.

493
00:47:52,773 --> 00:47:56,771
Under strange circumstances I
heard your name called out...

494
00:47:56,986 --> 00:47:58,876
...Ram!

495
00:47:59,092 --> 00:48:02,036
Not many days ago, a flying
chariot, swift as a wind...

496
00:48:02,253 --> 00:48:04,143
...raced above our heads
and we heard...

497
00:48:04,358 --> 00:48:07,302
...and we heard a lady's
cry for help...

498
00:48:07,517 --> 00:48:10,461
Ram... she cried. Help me Ram!

499
00:48:10,677 --> 00:48:13,621
From the chariot, a small
bundle dropped to the ground.

500
00:48:13,837 --> 00:48:17,835
We've kept it very carefully.
- Where is it? Where is it?

501
00:48:21,208 --> 00:48:24,152
Oh brother, look...

502
00:48:24,368 --> 00:48:27,311
...indeed they are her scarf...

503
00:48:27,526 --> 00:48:29,418
...and the ornaments
in her hair.

504
00:48:29,633 --> 00:48:33,631
Oh Sita... my Sita.

505
00:48:33,846 --> 00:48:37,844
Courage brother, Ram.

506
00:48:38,059 --> 00:48:39,949
You have no time to grieve.
You must act without delay.

507
00:48:40,164 --> 00:48:44,162
I have sworn to rescue Sita
wherever she may be.

508
00:48:45,254 --> 00:48:48,378
Hmm, too well I know
how it hurts...

509
00:48:48,590 --> 00:48:50,480
...to be without one's consort.

510
00:48:50,696 --> 00:48:53,640
My brother Bali, banished
me from my kingdom...

511
00:48:53,855 --> 00:48:55,745
...then usurped my wife.

512
00:48:55,961 --> 00:48:59,918
Oh, if only I had the kingdom's
army at my disposal...

513
00:49:00,131 --> 00:49:02,003
...I would send my men to search
the whole world...

514
00:49:02,216 --> 00:49:05,129
...to rescue your wife, Sita.

515
00:49:05,342 --> 00:49:08,256
Look, let us make this
government, O Prince of Ayodhya...

516
00:49:08,470 --> 00:49:11,383
Let us forge our strength in
friendship and swear to relieve...

517
00:49:11,596 --> 00:49:14,511
...the sorrows that have
befallen us both. - Yes, let us.

518
00:49:15,592 --> 00:49:17,642
For the sake of a friend...

519
00:49:17,851 --> 00:49:21,808
...a man should be ready to
give up his wealth...

520
00:49:22,021 --> 00:49:24,935
...and comforts and if
need be life itself.

521
00:49:25,147 --> 00:49:28,061
I will live by this Dharm and...

522
00:49:28,275 --> 00:49:30,147
...help Ram in every way.

523
00:49:30,360 --> 00:49:33,273
I swear it. - I swear it too.

524
00:49:34,530 --> 00:49:38,487
Ram fulfilled the promise given
to Sugriva and forked the mighty Bali.

525
00:49:39,741 --> 00:49:43,698
Bali was defeated and Sugriva
regained his wife and his kingdom.

526
00:49:43,910 --> 00:49:46,824
The monsoon clouds gathered
like a herd of elephants...

527
00:49:47,039 --> 00:49:49,952
...and reclaimed the Rishyamukha
hills for many days.

528
00:49:58,504 --> 00:50:01,417
And when the rain ceased and
the sun shone again Rishyamukha...

529
00:50:01,631 --> 00:50:05,588
...stood like an island.
surrounded by the waters of the flood.

530
00:50:08,928 --> 00:50:11,841
And Sugriva called forth his
great army of monkeys.

531
00:50:12,054 --> 00:50:13,926
When you find my Sita, give
her these ornaments...

532
00:50:14,140 --> 00:50:17,054
...so she may recognize you
as my emissaries.

533
00:50:38,114 --> 00:50:42,071
These are the jewels of my
clan. Please give them to her.

534
00:50:52,534 --> 00:50:55,625
The vanara king Sugriva sent
search parties in all directions...

535
00:50:55,835 --> 00:50:57,706
...keeping his promise to Ram.

536
00:51:19,809 --> 00:51:21,681
Help... it's a tiger. Help!

537
00:51:36,313 --> 00:51:38,363
Look... look... over there.

538
00:51:38,572 --> 00:51:41,486
If a bird came out of that cave, there
might be some water inside.

539
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:44,613
Yes, perhaps we will
find some water there.

540
00:52:06,542 --> 00:52:08,591
They have gone inside.
- Gone inside now.

541
00:52:26,521 --> 00:52:28,392
Hey, I can see some light.

542
00:52:30,691 --> 00:52:32,562
That must be the way out. C'mon.

543
00:52:37,988 --> 00:52:40,901
Hanuman, who leads the
party to the south...

544
00:52:41,115 --> 00:52:42,986
...meets Sampaati...

545
00:52:43,200 --> 00:52:46,114
...brother of Jatayu...

546
00:52:46,326 --> 00:52:49,240
...the bird king, killed at
the hands of Ravan.

547
00:52:49,454 --> 00:52:51,326
Where are we?

548
00:52:58,835 --> 00:53:03,836
Are you not Jatayu's
brother, Sampaati!?

549
00:53:09,259 --> 00:53:13,216
Yes, I am Sampaati.

550
00:53:13,428 --> 00:53:16,341
Do you know my brother?

551
00:53:16,556 --> 00:53:19,470
How is my Jatayu?

552
00:53:20,551 --> 00:53:22,600
Is he well?

553
00:53:22,810 --> 00:53:25,724
Jatayu has found a
home in the heavens.

554
00:53:31,149 --> 00:53:33,020
Oh... how sad!

555
00:53:34,103 --> 00:53:36,152
How sad!

556
00:53:37,229 --> 00:53:40,322
My brother to die...

557
00:53:41,573 --> 00:53:45,530
...and I live on.

558
00:53:45,742 --> 00:53:48,655
Old though he was...

559
00:53:48,870 --> 00:53:52,826
...he fought a difficult battle
with an evil demon, Ravan...

560
00:53:53,908 --> 00:53:56,998
...and was slain as he
tried to save...

561
00:53:57,208 --> 00:54:01,165
...Mother Sita from
the demon's clutches?

562
00:54:01,377 --> 00:54:05,335
You said Ravan!?
Ravan is the name!?

563
00:54:05,547 --> 00:54:08,439
If I knew he had
killed my brother...

564
00:54:08,652 --> 00:54:11,543
...I would never have let him...

565
00:54:11,755 --> 00:54:13,612
...fly over this land, unharmed.

566
00:54:14,686 --> 00:54:16,719
He flew over here?

567
00:54:16,928 --> 00:54:18,785
Yes, look...

568
00:54:19,858 --> 00:54:21,892
...across the sea...

569
00:54:22,100 --> 00:54:24,991
...is Lanka.

570
00:54:26,066 --> 00:54:29,133
There you will find...

571
00:54:30,203 --> 00:54:34,295
...and his captive the lady.

572
00:54:34,513 --> 00:54:37,405
If we cross the sea
with all the troops...

573
00:54:37,617 --> 00:54:39,475
...we will need
thousands of boats.

574
00:54:40,548 --> 00:54:43,617
And I am too old now.

575
00:54:43,825 --> 00:54:47,752
Though in my youth I had
circled the earth 21 times.

576
00:54:50,894 --> 00:54:52,927
Now, there is only
one among us...

577
00:54:53,134 --> 00:54:54,992
...who can handle this task.

578
00:54:56,066 --> 00:54:58,100
When you were a boy...

579
00:54:58,307 --> 00:55:01,199
...believing the new born sun
to be a golden fruit...

580
00:55:01,410 --> 00:55:04,303
...you once flew after it...

581
00:55:04,515 --> 00:55:06,372
...meaning to swallow it up.

582
00:55:06,583 --> 00:55:08,440
You had great powers...

583
00:55:08,654 --> 00:55:12,580
...but you did not
know how to use them.

584
00:55:13,653 --> 00:55:16,721
The world was afraid of you...

585
00:55:16,756 --> 00:55:19,825
...and so you were put
under a spell...

586
00:55:20,032 --> 00:55:21,889
...that sealed your powers.

587
00:55:22,102 --> 00:55:24,993
But the time has now
come for me...

588
00:55:25,205 --> 00:55:27,062
...to unseal these
hidden powers.

589
00:55:28,136 --> 00:55:32,228
Only you can cross the sea
with your divine powers.

590
00:55:32,447 --> 00:55:36,373
Only you can reach Lanka
and find mother Sita.

591
00:56:21,931 --> 00:56:23,964
I... can fly!

592
00:56:30,207 --> 00:56:33,275
He has done it... he has done
it! How wonderful!

593
00:56:37,621 --> 00:56:41,548
Farewell prince!

594
00:56:48,828 --> 00:56:50,861
Hanuman rushes towards Lanka...

595
00:56:51,070 --> 00:56:53,961
...but is challenged by the
sea monster Sindhika.

596
00:56:55,035 --> 00:56:57,068
What's that?

597
00:57:34,347 --> 00:57:36,381
Where am I?

598
00:57:37,623 --> 00:57:39,480
I must get out of here.

599
00:57:59,348 --> 00:58:03,275
Now I will cut you up
to little pieces.

600
00:58:04,347 --> 00:58:10,840
After a furious battle Hanuman
tears the monster to pieces...

601
00:58:10,840 --> 00:58:13,772
...and proceeds towards the
island of Lanka.

602
01:00:12,284 --> 01:00:15,395
But where on earth do I find Sita?

603
01:00:52,300 --> 01:00:54,182
Ah... you are awake.

604
01:00:55,270 --> 01:00:59,417
My day begins only when I see
the radiance of your face.

605
01:00:59,640 --> 01:01:02,570
But you... you won't
even look at me.

606
01:01:02,785 --> 01:01:04,418
Do you not see I am starving
for your love?

607
01:01:05,513 --> 01:01:08,056
Perhaps I should make a
gift of Ram's head.

608
01:01:08,242 --> 01:01:09,876
So, you have visited
her again.

609
01:01:10,062 --> 01:01:11,446
Leave her alone, my Lord.

610
01:01:11,603 --> 01:01:13,756
Let's sing and dance over
there. Let's make merry.

611
01:01:16,098 --> 01:01:21,969
There is only a little time left.
The promise, dear, will soon be over.

612
01:01:28,028 --> 01:01:30,380
Huh! How on earth is our
lord attracted by you?

613
01:01:30,552 --> 01:01:32,904
I wonder what he sees in you!?

614
01:01:33,076 --> 01:01:35,428
I would like to see your husband.
I can't imagine anyone...

615
01:01:35,601 --> 01:01:37,952
...more handsome than the
Lord of Lanka.

616
01:01:38,125 --> 01:01:39,635
Go away all of you.
Do not annoy Sita...

617
01:01:39,807 --> 01:01:41,317
...or I will have to
answer to Ravan.

618
01:01:49,903 --> 01:01:52,256
O Ram! Ram, my husband...

619
01:01:53,129 --> 01:01:54,783
...come to save me quickly.

620
01:01:55,653 --> 01:01:57,307
O Ram!

621
01:02:05,978 --> 01:02:10,629
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

622
01:02:11,858 --> 01:02:16,509
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

623
01:02:17,738 --> 01:02:22,692
I bow at your feet...

624
01:02:22,904 --> 01:02:26,699
...having this great
opportunity with me.

625
01:02:26,903 --> 01:02:30,699
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

626
01:02:30,903 --> 01:02:35,698
O mother, I am
Ram's emissary.

627
01:02:46,735 --> 01:02:50,899
The radiance of my Lord is
like the shining sun...

628
01:02:51,999 --> 01:02:56,164
...and his voice is as soothing
as the moonlight.

629
01:02:57,263 --> 01:03:01,428
You have been
abducted by Ravan...

630
01:03:01,651 --> 01:03:04,594
...and he has called for his
own death by doing so.

631
01:03:04,810 --> 01:03:09,860
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

632
01:03:10,074 --> 01:03:15,124
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

633
01:03:26,746 --> 01:03:30,910
My Lord remains deep in
thought, each moment.

634
01:03:31,133 --> 01:03:35,130
But he constantly
thinks about you only.

635
01:03:36,222 --> 01:03:40,385
His eyes are always longing...

636
01:03:40,610 --> 01:03:43,552
...to see you, that's
my own knowledge.

637
01:03:43,768 --> 01:04:03,046
O mother, I am the
emissary of Ram.

638
01:04:06,256 --> 01:04:10,196
Come with me, mother.
I will take you back to Ram.

639
01:04:10,406 --> 01:04:13,309
I can't go with you. There
are many people in Lanka...

640
01:04:13,521 --> 01:04:16,422
...who have been abducted
and enslaved by force.

641
01:04:16,635 --> 01:04:19,536
I'm not the only one who
is to be rescued.

642
01:04:20,613 --> 01:04:22,653
Hmm... I understand.
I am leaving now.

643
01:04:22,862 --> 01:04:25,763
But soon your beloved
husband Ram will defeat...

644
01:04:25,976 --> 01:04:28,876
...Ravan and release
the people of Lanka.

645
01:04:29,089 --> 01:04:33,029
Take heart, be courageous, till
the day of liberty comes.

646
01:04:33,241 --> 01:04:36,142
Tell Ram to come and
save me quickly.

647
01:04:36,353 --> 01:04:39,254
I will be hopeful till then.
- I will surely tell him.

648
01:04:41,370 --> 01:04:45,475
Before I leave, I must teach
Ravan and his friends a lesson.

649
01:04:48,635 --> 01:04:50,570
Besides, I need the exercise.

650
01:05:04,233 --> 01:05:05,242
Douse the fire!

651
01:05:11,546 --> 01:05:13,599
The next one promises to be
a better match for me.

652
01:05:24,084 --> 01:05:26,137
Perhaps, if I let myself
to be captured...

653
01:05:27,216 --> 01:05:31,350
...I will be able to see Ravan
himself, face to face.

654
01:05:32,441 --> 01:05:34,567
Help! I can't stand the fire.

655
01:05:38,931 --> 01:05:42,141
You there!? What is
your name and...

656
01:05:42,358 --> 01:05:45,380
...who has sent you to Lanka?

657
01:05:52,095 --> 01:05:55,117
O Lord of Lanka, I am Hanuman.

658
01:05:55,339 --> 01:05:58,977
I come to you with respect as
a messenger of Lord Sugriva...

659
01:05:59,174 --> 01:06:03,772
...the Vanara King and devoted
friend of Ram, Prince of Ayodhya.

660
01:06:03,968 --> 01:06:07,606
You know it was a cowardly act
to carry off Princess Sita.

661
01:06:07,803 --> 01:06:09,525
Totally contrary to Dharm.

662
01:06:10,518 --> 01:06:12,403
This will surely end in
your destruction...

663
01:06:12,597 --> 01:06:14,318
...and the destruction
of your race.

664
01:06:16,271 --> 01:06:20,062
Restore Sita to the prince
and seek his forgiveness.

665
01:06:22,023 --> 01:06:23,907
Kill him.

666
01:06:25,858 --> 01:06:28,022
Brother, according to the law of kings,
you may mutilate, brand or whip...

667
01:06:28,243 --> 01:06:30,218
...a messenger, but kill him?

668
01:06:30,443 --> 01:06:34,619
Why? What's wrong in killing a
creature such as this?

669
01:06:34,844 --> 01:06:37,920
If you slay him, what
chance is there...

670
01:06:38,143 --> 01:06:40,118
...of our real enemies
being brought here?

671
01:06:41,444 --> 01:06:44,519
All right, but set fire to his
tail first. Then let him go home.

672
01:06:52,447 --> 01:06:55,520
Oh... it's hot. It's
burning me. Help!

673
01:07:01,063 --> 01:07:01,677
It's hot... it's hot...
it's hot...

674
01:07:02,001 --> 01:07:02,615
...it's hot... it's hot...
- Stop him! Stop him!

675
01:07:51,087 --> 01:07:55,499
Ravan, my brother, I have come
to beg you. Return Sita...

676
01:07:55,737 --> 01:07:58,854
...to Ram or I fear the next
time not only the city...

677
01:07:59,081 --> 01:08:01,086
...but the palace itself
will go up in flames.

678
01:08:02,243 --> 01:08:07,771
You spoke this. If anyone else
had the gall to speak to me like...

679
01:08:08,006 --> 01:08:11,126
...this, I might have killed him
on the spot. I... King Ravan, who...

680
01:08:11,353 --> 01:08:14,471
...has won the obedience of all
men and the praises of the Gods ...

681
01:08:14,699 --> 01:08:18,978
...you expect me to shiver
from fear of a mere princeling?

682
01:08:19,161 --> 01:08:23,150
Be gone treacherous one.
Get out. Get out of my sight.

683
01:08:35,803 --> 01:08:38,920
Quiet! Quiet! How do we
cross over to the...

684
01:08:39,131 --> 01:08:42,070
...other side? - We will need
thousands of boats for these great troops.

685
01:08:43,161 --> 01:08:45,214
Then we can build a bridge.
- A bridge!? Do you know...

686
01:08:45,423 --> 01:08:48,343
...how many years it will take
to construct such a long bridge?

687
01:08:49,427 --> 01:08:52,525
If it is only mother Sita to be
rescued, I would fly to Lanka...

688
01:08:52,735 --> 01:08:54,939
...and accomplish the mission
myself quite easily.

689
01:08:55,153 --> 01:08:58,056
We have to rescue not only
Sita but others too.

690
01:08:58,269 --> 01:09:00,134
Ravan must be
destroyed or else...

691
01:09:00,347 --> 01:09:03,250
...there will be no lasting
peace on earth.

692
01:09:06,407 --> 01:09:09,487
Listen all of you. A demon,
named Vibhishana...

693
01:09:09,696 --> 01:09:12,601
...a brother of Ravan, comes
in peace, seeking refuge.

694
01:09:17,833 --> 01:09:21,943
He disagreed with his brother
and protected me in Ravan's palace.

695
01:09:22,163 --> 01:09:25,067
I have observed his honest
nature for myself.

696
01:09:25,279 --> 01:09:28,183
I see no fault in his
joining our forces.

697
01:09:28,395 --> 01:09:31,300
I agree with Hanuman.

698
01:09:32,378 --> 01:09:34,420
You are now amongst friends.

699
01:09:34,629 --> 01:09:36,493
Bless me, O Lord.

700
01:09:37,573 --> 01:09:41,681
I have overheard your
discussion on how to cross over...

701
01:09:41,901 --> 01:09:44,804
...to Lanka. I'd like to
suggest you pray to the Sea God for His help.

702
01:09:45,018 --> 01:09:46,882
That's good advice,
Vibhishana.

703
01:09:50,039 --> 01:09:53,150
For seven days and
seven nights...

704
01:09:53,361 --> 01:09:56,295
...Ram prayed to the Sea God.

705
01:10:01,580 --> 01:10:04,692
On the eighth dawn, the
God revealed Himself.

706
01:10:25,714 --> 01:10:30,912
Righteous Ram, build a
bridge with stones.

707
01:10:31,135 --> 01:10:35,119
Inscribe your name on each
stone and the stones will not...

708
01:10:35,331 --> 01:10:38,265
...sink in the ocean.

709
01:10:38,480 --> 01:10:41,413
Instead they will support
not only monkeys...

710
01:10:42,502 --> 01:10:45,614
...but all the living
creatures on the mountains...

711
01:10:46,698 --> 01:10:51,899
...and in the seas shall help
you build this bridge.

712
01:10:52,121 --> 01:10:55,054
And the Gods will bless
you with success.

713
01:11:01,564 --> 01:11:05,549
Now... let's start! Let us
build the bridge.

714
01:11:06,637 --> 01:11:08,672
Hail! Hail!

715
01:11:08,880 --> 01:11:12,807
A bridge was built...

716
01:11:13,019 --> 01:11:17,981
...in the name of Ram.

717
01:11:19,054 --> 01:11:23,146
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean...

718
01:11:24,228 --> 01:11:28,319
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean...

719
01:11:29,401 --> 01:11:33,494
...a bridge was built...

720
01:11:34,575 --> 01:11:38,668
...in the name of Ram.

721
01:11:41,818 --> 01:11:45,911
All the stones and rocks...

722
01:11:46,992 --> 01:11:51,085
...were collected to
make the bridge.

723
01:11:51,303 --> 01:11:55,231
On the heart of the ocean...

724
01:11:55,443 --> 01:11:59,370
...they were laid...

725
01:11:59,582 --> 01:12:03,509
On the heart of the ocean...

726
01:12:03,720 --> 01:12:06,612
...they were laid...

727
01:12:06,825 --> 01:12:09,715
...with the blessings of the
feet of Raghupati (Ram)...

728
01:12:09,928 --> 01:12:11,786
...with the blessings of the
feet of Raghupati...

729
01:12:11,998 --> 01:12:14,890
...and by his mere touch...

730
01:12:15,102 --> 01:12:19,030
...the stones started
floating in the sea.

731
01:12:20,103 --> 01:12:23,172
A bridge was built...

732
01:12:24,242 --> 01:12:29,369
...in the name of Ram.

733
01:12:35,623 --> 01:12:39,800
Just as the
stones kept floating...

734
01:12:40,024 --> 01:12:47,202
...so does the name of Ram,
floats one in this sea of life.

735
01:12:48,297 --> 01:12:52,474
A remembrance of the
glorious tale of Ram...

736
01:12:53,578 --> 01:12:57,755
...a remembrance of the
glorious tale of Ram...

737
01:12:58,858 --> 01:13:03,036
...is sufficient to give
success in all the endeavors.

738
01:13:03,259 --> 01:13:08,325
Devotion towards Ram
is the key to success.

739
01:13:08,540 --> 01:13:13,605
Just the name of Ram is
enough to settle all matters.

740
01:13:14,700 --> 01:13:17,834
A bridge was built...

741
01:13:19,101 --> 01:13:23,112
...in the name of Ram.

742
01:13:24,383 --> 01:13:28,392
On the heart of the sea,
across the ocean, a bridge was built...

743
01:13:29,488 --> 01:13:33,665
...in the name of Ram.

744
01:13:39,168 --> 01:13:42,079
Members of the council,
we are facing...

745
01:13:42,293 --> 01:13:45,203
...an outbreak of war.

746
01:13:45,417 --> 01:13:47,287
What do you have
to say, Prahastha?

747
01:13:48,367 --> 01:13:52,486
Your Majesty, you as the
great lord of Lanka...

748
01:13:52,707 --> 01:13:56,660
...need not have called this
council just to consider...

749
01:13:56,872 --> 01:14:00,825
...this ridiculous threat, from
a handful of men and monkeys.

750
01:14:01,905 --> 01:14:04,994
Just send a couple of my men...

751
01:14:05,204 --> 01:14:07,073
...who are not even present
in this council...

752
01:14:08,154 --> 01:14:11,242
...and they will surely
wipe out Ram's army.

753
01:14:11,452 --> 01:14:13,321
Ravan...

754
01:14:13,535 --> 01:14:17,488
...I told you before but now I
have to repeat it. Those who...

755
01:14:17,701 --> 01:14:22,696
...govern the kingdom should
never be swayed by flattery.

756
01:14:23,775 --> 01:14:26,863
The armies attacking us are
no ordinary ones.

757
01:14:27,941 --> 01:14:31,029
Ravan, I will tell you this
for your own good.

758
01:14:32,107 --> 01:14:35,195
Return Sita, she is the wife
of the Prince of Ayodhya.

759
01:14:35,404 --> 01:14:37,274
Grandfather...

760
01:14:39,396 --> 01:14:43,515
...why do we have to return
her now? If we release her now...

761
01:14:43,736 --> 01:14:47,689
...they will think that we
are all afraid of fighting.

762
01:14:48,769 --> 01:14:51,858
That is not so!? I cannot
bear the sight of...

763
01:14:52,067 --> 01:14:56,020
...so many people injured
and even more dead...

764
01:14:57,100 --> 01:14:59,147
...just for this one woman.

765
01:14:59,357 --> 01:15:03,310
Grandfather, that means you
are afraid of fighting.

766
01:15:04,390 --> 01:15:07,479
If you are scared of bloodshed
how can you fight?

767
01:15:07,688 --> 01:15:11,641
Indrajeet, I am no coward.

768
01:15:11,854 --> 01:15:15,807
But yes, I don't want
to fight unnecessarily.

769
01:15:17,928 --> 01:15:23,089
You called me, O Ram.
- Yes, brave Prince of the Vanaras...

770
01:15:23,309 --> 01:15:26,220
...please, listen to what
I have to say, carefully.

771
01:15:29,383 --> 01:15:31,431
For these many months...

772
01:15:31,641 --> 01:15:33,510
...I've been thinking of
only defeating Ravan.

773
01:15:33,723 --> 01:15:36,634
Now my dream is about to
come true, however...

774
01:15:38,757 --> 01:15:42,876
...I have considered this matter
over and over again and...

775
01:15:44,138 --> 01:15:48,091
...I've concluded that I can
stop this fight even now...

776
01:15:48,302 --> 01:15:52,256
...if my wife Sita and other
captives are released...

777
01:15:52,468 --> 01:15:55,379
...and they ask for
shelter under me.

778
01:15:58,543 --> 01:16:01,632
Quiet! - You are, no
doubt, surprised, but...

779
01:16:02,709 --> 01:16:04,756
... shedding of blood
should be avoided...

780
01:16:04,965 --> 01:16:07,876
... and real peace should come
back to the three worlds.

781
01:16:08,089 --> 01:16:09,959
To ensure this...

782
01:16:10,172 --> 01:16:13,084
...I am ready to forgive and
forget the misdeeds of Ravan.

783
01:16:14,164 --> 01:16:17,253
Angad, could you carry
this message to Ravan?

784
01:16:21,454 --> 01:16:24,542
I... I understand. I will
surely convey your message...

785
01:16:24,752 --> 01:16:26,621
...to Ravan.
- Thank you, Angad.

786
01:16:34,992 --> 01:16:38,081
Is that all you
have to say to me?

787
01:16:39,157 --> 01:16:43,276
Well... Angad... that's
your name, isn't it?

788
01:16:44,365 --> 01:16:46,412
Here is my answer.

789
01:16:48,704 --> 01:16:50,574
How despicable!

790
01:16:50,787 --> 01:16:53,698
Is this how you treat a
messenger who comes in peace?

791
01:17:05,193 --> 01:17:06,199
Ravan...

792
01:17:08,317 --> 01:17:12,436
...Ravan, I have your answer.
And now I will carry your answer...

793
01:17:12,657 --> 01:17:16,610
...to Ram. Next time I see you,
it will be on the battlefield.

794
01:17:19,773 --> 01:17:22,862
So, Ravan wants war, after all.

795
01:17:23,070 --> 01:17:25,982
I understand. Angad,
I appreciate your endeavor.

796
01:17:26,194 --> 01:17:29,106
I am sorry, Ram,
but Ravan did not accept...

797
01:17:29,319 --> 01:17:32,230
...your message of peace.
I did my best.

798
01:17:38,691 --> 01:17:41,603
Now, tomorrow morning...

799
01:17:41,815 --> 01:17:43,685
...when the first rays of the
sun touch the mountaintops...

800
01:17:44,767 --> 01:17:46,813
...the battle will begin.

801
01:17:47,023 --> 01:17:48,892
I ask all of you present here...

802
01:17:49,973 --> 01:17:54,092
...will you fight for
justice and for Ram?

803
01:17:54,312 --> 01:17:58,266
All hail to Ram!
All hail to Sugriva!

804
01:17:58,478 --> 01:18:01,389
Hail! Hail! Hail!

805
01:18:47,251 --> 01:18:50,339
Hail to the great
lord of Lanka.

806
01:18:51,417 --> 01:18:54,505
Hail to the great
lord of Lanka.

807
01:18:55,581 --> 01:18:59,700
If anyone tries to get in
a scuffle with Ravan...

808
01:18:59,922 --> 01:19:03,875
If anyone tries to get in
a scuffle with Ravan...

809
01:19:04,086 --> 01:19:09,082
...he is sure to die
a dog's death.

810
01:19:09,294 --> 01:19:13,247
...he is sure to die
a dog's death.

811
01:19:13,459 --> 01:19:17,412
Hail to the king who
has ten lives.

812
01:19:18,493 --> 01:19:21,581
Hail to the king who
has ten lives.

813
01:19:24,741 --> 01:19:28,860
He kills all his
enemies in no time.

814
01:19:29,080 --> 01:19:33,033
He kills all the enemies!

815
01:19:33,246 --> 01:19:37,199
Hail to the king of demons!

816
01:19:37,412 --> 01:19:42,406
Hail to the king of demons!

817
01:19:45,570 --> 01:19:49,689
I pray to you, O Gods,
I pray to you.

818
01:19:50,755 --> 01:19:54,874
Please... please... protect Ram.
Protect my husband.

819
01:20:54,025 --> 01:20:56,072
Oh, what a nuisance!
This is bothering me.

820
01:21:36,724 --> 01:21:38,594
The day began well
for us, O King.

821
01:21:38,811 --> 01:21:42,764
But now the two armies
seem equally matched.

822
01:21:42,986 --> 01:21:44,856
Our men are beginning to tire.

823
01:21:45,942 --> 01:21:50,061
Let them withdraw
at once then and rest.

824
01:21:50,292 --> 01:21:54,245
Respected one, that will
only lead to our defeat.

825
01:21:54,466 --> 01:21:58,419
Let us send Kumbhakarna's sons,
Kumbha and Nikumbha.

826
01:21:59,509 --> 01:22:01,557
Tired soldiers can
fall back to defense...

827
01:22:01,771 --> 01:22:04,682
...but we shall keep up
pressure on our enemies...

828
01:22:04,902 --> 01:22:07,813
...until sunset. - Yes, at
sunset, Ram will stop the battle...

829
01:22:08,032 --> 01:22:13,027
...for the day to
attend to the wounded...

830
01:22:13,250 --> 01:22:17,203
...and to cremate the
dead with honor. - Good.

831
01:22:17,425 --> 01:22:19,295
I will send forth
Kumbha and Nikumbha.

832
01:22:25,774 --> 01:22:28,686
Here I come...
monkeys, down with you.

833
01:22:31,862 --> 01:22:33,909
I will crush you to crumbs.

834
01:22:38,124 --> 01:22:40,170
O my God!

835
01:23:02,126 --> 01:23:04,174
Monkeys...

836
01:23:05,257 --> 01:23:07,305
...I will kill you.

837
01:23:17,955 --> 01:23:20,865
Your Majesty,
Kumbha and Nikumbha...

838
01:23:21,086 --> 01:23:23,996
...are fighting with great
courage on the battlefield.

839
01:23:24,216 --> 01:23:28,170
Well, after all, they are
the sons of Kumbhakarna.

840
01:23:32,393 --> 01:23:34,440
So many dead!

841
01:23:35,523 --> 01:23:37,571
So many wounded!

842
01:23:42,830 --> 01:23:45,919
Have you got the
water ready? - Yes.

843
01:23:46,135 --> 01:23:48,005
Medicines? Herbs?
- Yes, they are ready.

844
01:23:49,092 --> 01:23:52,181
Let's get the bed set fast.
C'mon quickly. - Yeah.

845
01:24:02,835 --> 01:24:05,746
Hey, more herbs.

846
01:24:06,835 --> 01:24:08,883
There are so many wounded.

847
01:24:27,711 --> 01:24:31,830
You've fought bravely.
I am so proud of you.

848
01:24:32,930 --> 01:24:36,019
Now rest. - Oh no.
Such a tiny wound...

849
01:24:36,235 --> 01:24:39,146
...will be cured by
tomorrow, you will see.

850
01:24:42,323 --> 01:24:46,443
Do not strain yourself,
rest. - Yes... yes, sir.

851
01:25:02,328 --> 01:25:05,240
Brother, how could you
cremate the bodies of our...

852
01:25:05,459 --> 01:25:07,329
...enemies along with those
of our own soldiers?

853
01:25:08,417 --> 01:25:12,536
Lakshman, they were our men and
Ravan's men while they were alive.

854
01:25:12,766 --> 01:25:15,677
But in death they
are no longer enemies.

855
01:25:15,897 --> 01:25:18,809
Do they not all of them deserve
a solemn cremation?

856
01:25:19,898 --> 01:25:21,946
It is not like a true warrior...

857
01:25:22,154 --> 01:25:25,065
...a true Kshatriya, to be
moved by such emotion.

858
01:25:25,277 --> 01:25:29,231
My brother, when we set out
on this expedition...

859
01:25:30,482 --> 01:25:33,393
...I too was full
of anger, bitterness.

860
01:25:33,606 --> 01:25:36,517
But on our journey to Lanka,
I've come to see that all of us...

861
01:25:37,596 --> 01:25:41,715
...have received the precious
gift of life from the Gods.

862
01:25:42,975 --> 01:25:45,887
And it is more important to
be a good human being...

863
01:25:46,098 --> 01:25:49,005
...than to be just
a good Kshatriya.

864
01:25:50,256 --> 01:25:54,205
Have we not, all of us,
sprung from the same souls?

865
01:25:54,416 --> 01:25:57,323
Rakshash, vanar, men, beasts...

866
01:25:57,535 --> 01:26:00,442
...birds of the air,
the fish of the ocean...??

867
01:26:03,598 --> 01:26:06,683
Yet, some of us, in ignorance...

868
01:26:06,891 --> 01:26:09,799
...draw their bows and swords
against their fellow creatures.

869
01:26:11,916 --> 01:26:13,961
Many have fallen off
this battlefield today.

870
01:26:14,169 --> 01:26:17,076
And many more shall die
before the war is done.

871
01:26:17,287 --> 01:26:21,235
And as a Kshatriya, I shall
continue to fight my battles.

872
01:26:23,352 --> 01:26:26,437
But when I burn
the dead, I shall pray...

873
01:26:26,644 --> 01:26:29,552
...for a world free
from all wars.

874
01:26:30,629 --> 01:26:33,714
That a man does not
raise his hand in anger...

875
01:26:33,922 --> 01:26:35,789
...against his own brother.

876
01:26:39,986 --> 01:26:42,031
Brother, words fail me.

877
01:27:17,412 --> 01:27:20,498
I am Neel, the General
of the Vanaras.

878
01:27:20,705 --> 01:27:23,612
Try all you can.
I shall defeat you.

879
01:28:13,553 --> 01:28:17,667
You have fought well
but this is the end.

880
01:28:50,980 --> 01:28:51,985
Wait!

881
01:28:59,471 --> 01:29:02,379
Hail Sugriva! Hail Sugriva!

882
01:29:48,160 --> 01:29:51,245
Kumbha, Kumbha... my brother.

883
01:29:53,359 --> 01:29:55,404
Are you really gone?

884
01:29:59,770 --> 01:30:03,719
Is it you? Is it you who
killed my brother Kumbha?

885
01:30:04,795 --> 01:30:08,908
Yes, I am... I am Sugriva,
the king of the Vanaras.
    
886
01:30:09,126 --> 01:30:13,075
Your brother Kumbha was
really brave and courageous.

887
01:30:15,191 --> 01:30:18,276
I have never met such a
mighty opponent before.

888
01:30:18,483 --> 01:30:22,431
I am very impressed by his
tactics. Please cremate him in honor.

889
01:30:23,508 --> 01:30:26,593
Indrajeet, what are you
saying? Prahastha and Kumbha...

890
01:30:26,822 --> 01:30:29,730
...both have been killed?
- It is unfortunate but true.

891
01:30:32,929 --> 01:30:34,973
I never thought Ram's army
had anyone to match them.

892
01:30:36,069 --> 01:30:39,154
It's time to review our
strategy. It can be of help under the...

893
01:30:39,384 --> 01:30:42,291
...circumstances. Indrajeet,
arouse Kumbhakarna from his sleep.

894
01:30:42,523 --> 01:30:45,430
What? - Kumbha and Nikumbha
fought so hard.

895
01:30:45,664 --> 01:30:50,652
Now Kumbhakarna, their father,
ten times mightier than...

896
01:30:50,897 --> 01:30:53,804
...them can work wonders.
Yes, I am right, wake him up...

897
01:30:54,038 --> 01:30:55,905
...immediately.
This is my command.

898
01:30:56,131 --> 01:30:57,999
All right, father. I will.

899
01:31:08,517 --> 01:31:10,562
Forward.

900
01:32:09,228 --> 01:32:11,272
C'mon... yeah...

901
01:32:34,524 --> 01:32:35,351
Oh, that big giant!

902
01:32:36,443 --> 01:32:38,488
Our lord
Kumbhakarna has arrived.

903
01:32:56,331 --> 01:32:59,415
Father... father!

904
01:33:12,032 --> 01:33:15,116
Vibhishana, who is that
gigantic warrior? - That O Ram, is the...

905
01:33:15,347 --> 01:33:21,375
...best and the bravest
warrior of Ravan's troops. Kumbhakarna...

906
01:33:23,720 --> 01:33:26,628
...after six months' sleep, he
would have become immortal.

907
01:33:27,732 --> 01:33:31,846
But it seems to me that Ravan
was forced to wake up because...

908
01:33:32,094 --> 01:33:36,043
...he was in terror to see so
many of his soldiers killed one...

909
01:33:36,281 --> 01:33:40,230
...after the other. Oh yes, he
needs Kumbhakarna. But even he is...

910
01:33:40,467 --> 01:33:42,335
...not immortal. He is mighty
enough to make all the...

911
01:33:42,561 --> 01:33:44,428
... vanara soldiers run
away in panic...

912
01:33:44,655 --> 01:33:47,562
...by his appearance. But Ram...

913
01:33:47,795 --> 01:33:50,702
...now is the right moment for
you to go to battle.

914
01:33:53,551 --> 01:33:55,597
Now, we go to battle.

915
01:35:09,090 --> 01:35:10,957
Jump!

916
01:35:21,477 --> 01:35:24,562
Stop that!

917
01:35:25,664 --> 01:35:27,727
You are small but
you have courage.

918
01:35:32,001 --> 01:35:36,153
I am Angad, son of Bali.
The nephew of king Sugriva.

919
01:35:36,403 --> 01:35:39,337
You are kinsmen
of the Vanara king!?

920
01:35:40,452 --> 01:35:44,603
No wonder you fight so great.
But this is as far as you get...

921
01:35:44,853 --> 01:35:46,738
...against me. - Wait.

922
01:35:50,135 --> 01:35:55,169
This is now my mission.
I see you are Kumbhakarna.

923
01:35:55,416 --> 01:35:58,350
The mightiest warrior of Lanka.

924
01:35:58,585 --> 01:36:02,570
Now this Hanuman
is your opponent.

925
01:36:02,810 --> 01:36:05,744
Good... Good.

926
01:36:06,859 --> 01:36:08,923
But before we fight... here.

927
01:36:14,254 --> 01:36:17,367
Oh... Kumbha...
Nikumbha... my sons.

928
01:36:26,929 --> 01:36:33,180
Hanuman, I thank you for your
consideration. - It is nothing.

929
01:36:43,830 --> 01:36:45,893
I won't fight you with
bare hands because...

930
01:36:46,091 --> 01:36:50,076
...you are skillful enough to
fight with weapons in dead earnest.

931
01:37:32,013 --> 01:37:34,947
It was good for you
that I lost my mace.

932
01:37:35,144 --> 01:37:37,029
Now get up and fight.

933
01:37:37,232 --> 01:37:40,165
Wait... stop wherever you are.

934
01:37:40,362 --> 01:37:44,347
I am Ram, the Prince of
Ayodhya, son of Dashrath.

935
01:38:01,062 --> 01:38:03,125
Give away, you stupid fools!

936
01:38:04,367 --> 01:38:07,301
So you are Ram!?

937
01:38:08,368 --> 01:38:11,481
You are a skillful
swordsman, I hear.

938
01:38:11,673 --> 01:38:13,557
You are annoying me.

939
01:38:14,629 --> 01:38:17,743
Go away, play
with the monkeys.

940
01:38:27,154 --> 01:38:31,305
It has grown dark
and even with...

941
01:38:31,502 --> 01:38:34,436
...Kumbhakarna on the field the
battle goes on and on.

942
01:38:34,633 --> 01:38:37,567
Father, I will go to the
battlefield and bring you the report.

943
01:38:37,765 --> 01:38:39,649
Yes Indrajeet, my son, go.

944
01:39:13,076 --> 01:39:17,227
Excuse me Kumbhakarna,
I am only doing my duty.

945
01:39:36,036 --> 01:39:38,100
He has done it!
He has done it.

946
01:39:39,167 --> 01:39:41,231
Hail to the Prince of Ayodhya!

947
01:39:43,341 --> 01:39:47,493
Brother, are you well?
It has been a glorious deed!

948
01:39:48,561 --> 01:39:52,712
Yes... I am hurt but
well in spirit.

949
01:39:52,909 --> 01:39:55,843
I wish I had known
him as a friend.

950
01:39:56,040 --> 01:39:58,974
Vibhishana, I am sorry,
Kumbhakarna had to die at my hands.

951
01:40:08,390 --> 01:40:11,503
Save us... save us O Vanaras.

952
01:40:18,826 --> 01:40:21,940
Thank you, Lord Ram!

953
01:40:22,132 --> 01:40:24,017
Ram, the great!

954
01:40:25,089 --> 01:40:28,202
Freedom, at last!

955
01:40:30,308 --> 01:40:32,371
We are free!

956
01:40:32,568 --> 01:40:35,503
What? Even
Kumbhakarna is gone?

957
01:40:35,699 --> 01:40:38,633
This spells
disaster for Lanka.

958
01:40:38,831 --> 01:40:41,765
He was a fine warrior.

959
01:40:42,831 --> 01:40:45,945
It is sad, very sad.

960
01:40:46,136 --> 01:40:49,071
Father... do not despair.
Have faith.

961
01:40:49,242 --> 01:40:52,177
I have a plan.

962
01:40:52,349 --> 01:40:56,334
I will devastate Ram's troops.
I assure you of this.

963
01:40:57,353 --> 01:41:01,504
Well said, my son, well said.
My faith lies in you.

964
01:41:02,530 --> 01:41:04,594
Now go ahead. - Yes, father.

965
01:41:05,809 --> 01:41:08,743
Let us bring all of them in,
while it is still dark.

966
01:41:08,915 --> 01:41:10,799
Hurry... hurry.

967
01:41:15,127 --> 01:41:19,112
There will be many more
corpses for you to gather, my friend.

968
01:41:19,270 --> 01:41:23,253
How dare he speak this way?
I will show him.

969
01:41:23,412 --> 01:41:25,296
Wait! What is that?

970
01:41:29,623 --> 01:41:31,508
That is Sita.

971
01:41:37,734 --> 01:41:40,847
Hanuman, are you
alright? Angad!?

972
01:41:49,124 --> 01:41:53,275
Where is Ram?
Why is he such a coward?

973
01:41:55,336 --> 01:41:58,448
Ram... Ram...

974
01:41:59,478 --> 01:42:01,541
Sita... my queen!

975
01:42:03,619 --> 01:42:05,682
Here you are.

976
01:42:06,898 --> 01:42:08,782
Ram, watch carefully.

977
01:42:15,181 --> 01:42:19,166
Stop! Stop! STOP!

978
01:42:24,500 --> 01:42:29,534
Sita... Sita!

979
01:42:42,102 --> 01:42:43,986
Lakshman...

980
01:42:44,173 --> 01:42:47,106
...come... come...
come over here.

981
01:42:54,527 --> 01:42:58,511
Before I dispose of you, Ram,
I will give you...

982
01:42:58,668 --> 01:43:02,653
...enough time to hold a funeral
for your wife and your brother.

983
01:43:11,093 --> 01:43:12,978
Sita!

984
01:43:21,447 --> 01:43:24,382
May I talk with
you for a moment?

985
01:43:24,553 --> 01:43:28,538
We have almost used up all the
herbs around in this area.

986
01:43:28,695 --> 01:43:32,679
But they don't heal the wounds
inflicted by Indrajeet, at all.

987
01:43:32,837 --> 01:43:36,821
What? What news
is this? - O God!

988
01:43:37,841 --> 01:43:41,993
Oh... I have already lost
my beloved wife Sita...

989
01:43:42,156 --> 01:43:46,140
...and now... I am going to lose
my dear, dear brother, Lakshman.

990
01:43:47,160 --> 01:43:49,223
If I lose him, what else
would be left for me?

991
01:43:52,417 --> 01:43:55,530
Brace yourself, Ram. You
cannot grieve and fret like this.

992
01:43:55,746 --> 01:43:58,680
Your despair will damage the
morale of our troops more than the...

993
01:43:58,901 --> 01:44:02,885
...enemy's arrows. Please
do not worry, Ram.

994
01:44:03,106 --> 01:44:06,040
Sita surely must be alive.
- Alive? But I saw Sita...

995
01:44:06,260 --> 01:44:10,245
...slain before my own eyes.

996
01:44:10,465 --> 01:44:14,450
I know, it must be one of
Indrajeet's magic tricks.

997
01:44:14,671 --> 01:44:17,605
A magic trick? What? - Yes.

998
01:44:17,825 --> 01:44:20,759
And we must not allow his
tricks to perplex us.

999
01:44:20,980 --> 01:44:22,864
Your grief will only
give him strength.

1000
01:44:23,958 --> 01:44:28,110
Indrajeet's strength lies
in his magical powers.

1001
01:44:28,339 --> 01:44:32,323
The only way to take his
powers away from him is to...

1002
01:44:32,544 --> 01:44:35,478
...attack Indrajeet while he
performs his Tantrik rites...

1003
01:44:35,593 --> 01:44:36,535
...in the cave of Nikumbhila.

1004
01:44:36,749 --> 01:44:40,734
Indrajeet makes it a rule to
perform a religious ceremony.

1005
01:44:40,956 --> 01:44:43,889
He offers sacrifices to
the Goddess Nikumbhila.

1006
01:44:44,109 --> 01:44:47,043
From the evening hours
way until nightfall.

1007
01:44:47,264 --> 01:44:51,248
He gains his extraordinary
magical powers through this ceremony.

1008
01:44:52,345 --> 01:44:56,496
I see, now... we still have so many...

1009
01:44:56,726 --> 01:44:59,631
...soldiers wounded, my
brother Lakshman, for instance.

1010
01:45:00,715 --> 01:45:04,824
No, I think it would be very
hard for us to attack Nikumbhila...

1011
01:45:05,052 --> 01:45:06,917
...cave now. - Ram.

1012
01:45:09,041 --> 01:45:13,150
In... in the Himalayas...
- Yes the Himalayas...

1013
01:45:13,377 --> 01:45:17,321
... what about them? Rest,
Jamvant. Talk to me.

1014
01:45:19,448 --> 01:45:22,530
I know there are
some herbs there...

1015
01:45:23,612 --> 01:45:27,721
...that can heal our wounds,
in the Himalayas. - The Himalayas?

1016
01:45:30,029 --> 01:45:32,933
I am afraid... I am afraid
that is too far away.

1017
01:46:21,891 --> 01:46:27,039
I see... that must be
Ram's kingdom! Ayodhya!

1018
01:46:35,421 --> 01:46:37,463
The Himalayas!

1019
01:46:40,624 --> 01:46:42,668
O you Himalayas!

1020
01:46:43,919 --> 01:46:47,864
Sacred mountains! At last!

1021
01:47:37,864 --> 01:47:39,907
Ah Dronagiri, at last!

1022
01:47:49,485 --> 01:47:52,390
Now, I have to look for herbs.

1023
01:47:52,607 --> 01:47:55,512
Our army is in
desperate need of this.

1024
01:48:00,933 --> 01:48:03,837
Ah the herbs... there they are.

1025
01:48:11,341 --> 01:48:14,244
Uff... that was painful.

1026
01:48:27,992 --> 01:48:31,937
Good, the pain is gone.
I am healed.

1027
01:48:32,156 --> 01:48:36,099
These herbs were far better
than I ever expected.

1028
01:48:41,347 --> 01:48:44,429
But wait! Just a
handful of these herbs...

1029
01:48:44,655 --> 01:48:47,560
...won't be enough
to heal them all.

1030
01:48:49,705 --> 01:48:52,787
Now... let me think.

1031
01:48:59,109 --> 01:49:02,190
I will take one.
Yes, this tree is good enough.

1032
01:49:44,210 --> 01:49:46,075
This will be a landmark.

1033
01:49:57,617 --> 01:50:00,698
Now I will pick up...

1034
01:50:00,926 --> 01:50:03,830
...the whole mountain.

1035
01:50:37,319 --> 01:50:41,428
I pray to you O Gods!
Protect my master Lakshman...

1036
01:50:41,672 --> 01:50:43,537
...I am coming back
with the herbs.

1037
01:50:45,850 --> 01:50:50,834
Brother Lakshman, keep up
your fight for life a little longer.

1038
01:50:58,214 --> 01:51:01,296
Bear your pain with courage,
Lakshman. Take heart...

1039
01:51:01,523 --> 01:51:04,428
...Hanuman will soon be back
with the herbs that will heal you.

1040
01:51:11,797 --> 01:51:16,945
Ram... Ram...
- Lakshman... Lakshman.

1041
01:51:18,066 --> 01:51:22,175
There he is.
- Hanuman has come. - Hail! Hail!

1042
01:51:23,290 --> 01:51:27,399
Here comes Hanuman! - But
what has he got on his shoulders?

1043
01:51:28,514 --> 01:51:31,595
He is carrying something.
- That's a mountain he is carrying.

1044
01:51:31,822 --> 01:51:35,766
Along with the herbs, he has
brought the whole mountain.

1045
01:51:54,633 --> 01:51:57,715
Hanuman, the herbs are on
this mountain? - Yes.

1046
01:51:57,924 --> 01:52:01,867
Look for the landmarks where
I have stuck trees to the soil.

1047
01:52:02,079 --> 01:52:04,983
Hurry, apply the herbs
to Lakshman's wounds.

1048
01:52:06,062 --> 01:52:09,144
Yes, it's a miracle.

1049
01:52:15,413 --> 01:52:18,494
Herbs... herbs. - At last.

1050
01:52:26,841 --> 01:52:29,923
Brother Ram... - O Lakshman...

1051
01:52:30,131 --> 01:52:31,996
...you have
regained consciousness.

1052
01:52:36,365 --> 01:52:39,270
Hanuman, you too are a
beloved brother to me.

1053
01:52:46,581 --> 01:52:49,663
Hey... - Who is that?

1054
01:53:05,283 --> 01:53:07,325
Hey... what was that?

1055
01:53:14,634 --> 01:53:16,676
C'mon... c'mon.

1056
01:53:58,445 --> 01:54:00,310
What has happened?

1057
01:54:02,427 --> 01:54:04,469
Oh no... who is there?

1058
01:54:05,557 --> 01:54:08,656
Is it you? You are still alive.

1059
01:54:09,754 --> 01:54:14,932
Yes, and it is time for you
to die along with your guardian Goddess.

1060
01:54:19,375 --> 01:54:22,296
It is hard to believe
that even such one as you...

1061
01:54:22,523 --> 01:54:24,399
...can have faithful
slaves to save you.

1062
01:54:25,497 --> 01:54:28,595
All of you, kill him.

1063
01:55:00,127 --> 01:55:02,182
What a nuisance!

1064
01:55:08,523 --> 01:55:10,577
You... take me up there!

1065
01:55:43,155 --> 01:55:45,209
Indrajeet... - I am...

1066
01:55:45,427 --> 01:55:49,394
...not so stupid to be trapped
by a monkey like you!

1067
01:55:58,895 --> 01:56:00,950
He has slipped past.

1068
01:56:11,488 --> 01:56:15,622
Listen, you obey my commands
and I'll spare your life.

1069
01:56:15,861 --> 01:56:17,737
Carry me to the sky. Remember...

1070
01:56:17,960 --> 01:56:19,836
...you should head right,
when I say right...

1071
01:56:20,059 --> 01:56:22,980
...and left when I say left.
If you fail to do so...

1072
01:56:23,207 --> 01:56:26,128
...this sword
will cut your throat.

1073
01:56:49,268 --> 01:56:51,322
Lakshman... !!?

1074
01:56:52,417 --> 01:56:55,516
Just keep going...
and faster... faster.

1075
01:56:56,614 --> 01:56:58,669
I will kill you.

1076
01:57:02,910 --> 01:57:04,964
Not this time.
This time I will kill you.

1077
01:57:18,652 --> 01:57:20,706
You cannot destroy this.

1078
01:57:32,469 --> 01:57:36,436
But this is the end of you.

1079
01:57:38,591 --> 01:57:40,645
This is your end, not mine.

1080
01:57:44,887 --> 01:57:46,942
I've waited for this moment.

1081
01:57:52,234 --> 01:57:54,288
Got you, you little one.

1082
01:58:13,222 --> 01:58:16,322
This is the end of
the invincible Indrajeet.

1083
01:58:18,469 --> 01:58:22,601
No... never...
I wouldn't let you kill me.

1084
01:58:42,606 --> 01:58:45,706
O Indrajeet... my son.

1085
01:58:45,929 --> 01:58:49,896
My beloved son slew
an illusion of Sita.

1086
01:58:50,121 --> 01:58:53,042
I shall not slay the real one.

1087
01:58:53,264 --> 01:58:57,231
Anyone so devoted to
Ram deserves to die.

1088
01:58:58,330 --> 01:59:01,429
Will you now add to your
sins by killing Sita!?

1089
01:59:01,648 --> 01:59:03,524
An innocent woman!?

1090
01:59:03,744 --> 01:59:07,711
Look at Prahastha, look
at Kumbha... Nikumbha...

1091
01:59:07,936 --> 01:59:10,856
...and Kumbhakarna.
Each one fought bravely and...

1092
01:59:11,080 --> 01:59:12,956
...died a hero's death.
Even Indrajeet died...

1093
01:59:13,175 --> 01:59:17,142
...in battle. You who
are brother, father...

1094
01:59:17,367 --> 01:59:20,288
...king to them all...

1095
01:59:20,511 --> 01:59:22,387
...do you want
disgrace their memory?

1096
01:59:22,606 --> 01:59:25,528
The time has
come for both of us...

1097
01:59:25,750 --> 01:59:27,626
...to go forth
and avenge our kinsmen.

1098
01:59:29,768 --> 01:59:32,867
I understand. But you will stay
here and protect our women and...

1099
01:59:33,088 --> 01:59:36,008
...children. No power on earth
can crush me. Not even Ram's.

1100
02:00:30,549 --> 02:00:32,603
Fire and damnation!

1101
02:00:53,603 --> 02:00:55,657
He looks like Vishnu
himself on his Garuda.

1102
02:00:55,875 --> 02:00:57,751
You are right, he does.

1103
02:01:34,474 --> 02:01:38,599
This battle between you and
me shall be the end of it all.

1104
02:01:38,832 --> 02:01:41,747
Citizens of Lanka, take heed.

1105
02:01:42,842 --> 02:01:45,936
Your king Ravan, whom you
consider a symbol of eternal...

1106
02:01:46,154 --> 02:01:50,114
...power, watch him die at
the hands of a mere mortal.

1107
02:01:51,210 --> 02:01:55,335
Ram, just tell me where your
conceit comes from, huh?

1108
02:01:55,568 --> 02:01:59,528
Your boastful lips will never
speak such words again.

1109
02:01:59,752 --> 02:02:02,668
Brave soldiers of Lanka...

1110
02:02:02,890 --> 02:02:04,762
...you know only too well...

1111
02:02:04,982 --> 02:02:07,898
...who is the mightiest
of all, here!

1112
02:02:08,120 --> 02:02:11,036
C'mon Ran...

1113
02:02:11,259 --> 02:02:14,174
So be it, Ravan! Fight!

1114
02:03:05,477 --> 02:03:07,529
Incredible!

1115
02:03:14,021 --> 02:03:15,893
Now, he is dead.

1116
02:03:38,951 --> 02:03:42,044
I can't believe my own eyes.

1117
02:03:46,273 --> 02:03:48,323
You thought I was
finished, did you?

1118
02:03:51,502 --> 02:03:54,596
I would like to
lay my hands on you!

1119
02:04:21,839 --> 02:04:23,889
Let's see you
get out of that one.

1120
02:04:43,804 --> 02:04:46,898
What power is
this, greater than mine?

1121
02:04:55,485 --> 02:04:58,283
Oh, you are going
too far now, I tell you.

1122
02:05:21,419 --> 02:05:23,387
Don't you dare!

1123
02:05:28,446 --> 02:05:30,414
Give up, Ram... give up!

1124
02:05:56,555 --> 02:05:59,524
Om... peace... peace... peace!!!

1125
02:06:47,640 --> 02:06:52,600
May you rest in peace,
brother Ravan. - It is all over.

1126
02:07:00,151 --> 02:07:05,111
Soldiers of Lanka, king Ravan
has gone back to mother Earth.

1127
02:07:06,406 --> 02:07:08,374
Give up fighting.
Lay down your arms...

1128
02:07:08,666 --> 02:07:12,466
...and devote yourself to
restoring the glory of your country...

1129
02:07:12,836 --> 02:07:14,633
...with your new king Vibhishana.

1130
02:07:18,917 --> 02:07:20,885
Ram...

1131
02:07:35,598 --> 02:07:37,566
Sita! - Ram!

1132
02:07:48,109 --> 02:07:52,068
Thank you all, but when I think
of the people who died for me...

1133
02:07:53,322 --> 02:07:56,291
...I feel sad. I will meditate
and will pray for them from now on...

1134
02:07:56,623 --> 02:07:58,420
...and beg their forgiveness.

1135
02:07:59,577 --> 02:08:01,545
You don't need to do that.

1136
02:08:01,924 --> 02:08:04,722
All you need is to live
in peace with Ram...

1137
02:08:05,173 --> 02:08:06,970
...to make their death
a glorious sacrifice.

1138
02:08:07,339 --> 02:08:10,137
I will remember
what you said, Sugriva.

1139
02:08:13,657 --> 02:08:17,616
Vibhishana, the new king of
Lanka presents Ram and Sita...

1140
02:08:18,170 --> 02:08:20,968
... the Vimana, the flying
chariot, to return to Ayodhya.

1141
02:08:46,150 --> 02:08:50,109
As they return, Sita gazes
at Ram with mixed feelings.

1142
02:08:50,321 --> 02:08:53,119
Happy to be
reunited with him...

1143
02:08:53,324 --> 02:08:55,121
...after a long
period of separation.

1144
02:08:55,326 --> 02:08:59,126
And sorrowful too for the
precious lives lost for her sake...

1145
02:08:59,330 --> 02:09:01,127
...in the avoidable war.

1146
02:09:12,176 --> 02:09:15,145
Ayodhya celebrates the safe
return of their beloved king...

1147
02:09:15,346 --> 02:09:18,144
...and they live
happily thereafter.

1148
02:09:18,349 --> 02:09:21,147
A few years later,
Ram returns to the Heavens...

1149
02:09:21,352 --> 02:09:23,149
...while Sita
returns to Mother Earth.

